knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3761 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3758)
What it fixes: a `require()` in a branch that `process.env.NEXT_RUNTIME` makes dead was still
resolved, so `instrumentation.js` with `else { await require("this should fail") }` failed to
build (Next.js e2e `instrumentation-hook`, `with-esm-import`). vite-plugin-commonjs hoists every
`require()` to a top-level import before Rolldown applies the define and drops the branch. The
CommonJS transform wrapper now blanks such dead branches first (new
dist/plugins/next-runtime-dead-branches.js), keeping every offset, when the test only compares
NEXT_RUNTIME with string literals.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3761.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.1.0 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

